{"rules":[{"jurisdiction":"Cambridge, MA","level":"city","category":"screening_restrictions","status":"in_force","title":"Cambridge Fair Housing Ordinance: source of income (including Section 8) protected in tenant selection","requirement":"The Fair Housing Ordinance prohibits housing discrimination in renting, including on the basis of source of income, which the page says includes Section 8 and public benefits. Landlords, sellers and rental agents may use any reasonable standard to select applicants if it is applied equally and uniformly to all applicants. Tenant selection may be based on an applicant's ability to pay the rent and ability to take care of the apartment and respect the rights of others.","key_value":"Source of income, including Section 8 and public benefits, is a protected category","coverage_conditions":"Rental housing in Cambridge, including viewing or renting an apartment and terms and conditions of tenancy.","exemptions":"Exemption for 2-family dwellings when the owner lives there.","coverage_logic":{"covers":null,"exempt":{"all":[{"field":"units","op":"==","value":2},{"field":"owner_occupied","op":"==","value":true}]}},"subject":"landlord","interaction":null,"yields_to_local":false,"preempts_local":false,"effective_date":null,"effective_rule":null,"enacted_date":null,"end_date":null,"penalty":"The Commission may levy civil fines of up to $300 for each violation, file a criminal complaint in District Court, or file a civil complaint in Superior Court seeking injunctive relief, damages, expenses and other relief.","citation":"Cambridge Fair Housing Ordinance, chapter 14.04","quoted_span":"Under the law, landlords, sellers and rental agents may use any reasonable standard to determine which applicants are selected, as long as that standard is applied equally and uniformly to all applicants.","supporting_spans":["Source of Income, includes Section 8 and public benefits","NOTE: there is an exemption for 2-family dwellings, when the owner lives there"],"confidence":0.5,"conflict_note":null}],"notes":"This is an agency overview page, not the ordinance text. Only the source-of-income protection in the Cambridge Fair Housing Ordinance falls in scope, under screening_restrictions. The page gives no enactment or effective dates and no operative details beyond the summary. The page also links a Tenants' Rights and Resources Notification Ordinance, but describes no content for it, so it is not recorded. Nothing on the page covers rent increase limits, just cause eviction, security deposits, application or screening fees, or algorithmic rent setting."}
